---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_266",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 266,
  "text": "<p> [[817.6]] <b>231a. ROBERT HOOKE AN THEODOR HAAK FÜR LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[817.7]] [London, 13. April 1681.] [228a.]</b></p>\n<p> [[817.19]] S^#'r </p>\n<p> [[817.20]] I am extreamly pleasd to find soe excellent a Person as the Learned world must Acknowledg\n[[817.21]] M^#'r Leibnitz to concur in the same opinion w^#'t^#'h me that A language somew^#'t Like that of\n[[817.22]] y^#'e Bishop of Chester would be of use for the Promotion of Science. It has been Long my\n[[817.23]] Judgment, and that founded upon undenyable principles from w^#'c^#'h I cannot Recede that this\n[[817.24]] Language would be of much greater use then the world has conceived, though I have hitherto\n[[817.25]] had the Ill fortune scarcly to meet w^#'t^#'h one man (except himself) whom I can persuade to concurr\n[[817.26]] w^#'t^#'h me and that the Greatest number Look upon it only as a chymera and at best but a\n[[817.27]] Supplement for Latine in the inner parts of Europe or for the Lingua franca in the maritime, yet\n[[817.28]] my aymes have Always been much higher viz. to make it not only usefull for Expressing and\n[[817.29]] Remembring of things and notions but to Direct Regulate assist and even necessitate and\n[[818.1]] compell the mind to find out and comprehent whatsoever is knowable. And to make it an\n[[818.2]] Instrument which being actuated by the power of the mind shall most certainly produce the\n[[818.3]] Desired effect or plainly show the Impossibility thereof; especially in all those subjects where\n[[818.4]] y^#'e use of it may be free and where interest and Authority doe not Intercept the Regular Course\n[[818.5]] thereof, which I conceive to be the great antagonists which may impede its progress, preposession\n[[818.6]] may clogg it but it will get through safe and well: not withstanding. It may therefore not\n[[818.7]] unfitly be called the Algebra of Algebras or the Science of methods, which every one that now\n[[818.8]] Invents a particular method does somew^#'t participate but comes short of the full perfection and\n[[818.9]] best of that kind, at Least if he Light on it he knows not how he came by it nor can he prove that\n[[818.10]] tis soe and not otherwise. Any thing therefore that M^#'r Leibnitz knows that will promote this end\n[[818.11]] will be highly acceptable if he please to communicate it and shall be acknowledged as his. The\n[[818.12]] Great Difficulty lyes in the media but the Generall method will not only plainely show what\n[[818.13]] those are but the way of attaining them, but this is not to be done in many subjects but w^#'t^#'h much\n[[818.14]] exercise of the method and there is a subordination and positure in the subjects of Inquiry\n[[818.15]] themselves, and therefore the first Alphabet or those which may be called the Symbols are first\n[[818.16]] to be understood, then those which may be called the Syllables then the words then sentences or\n[[818.17]] propositions etc. nor is it to be imagined a Scollar in this art shall at first sight read perfectly\n[[818.18]] But must with Labour and Patience proceed methodically, and goe by steps from subject to\n[[818.19]] subject as Nature has placed them in order, and then tis not to be doubted but the Soule of man\n[[818.20]] may be carryed to the highest step of knowledge and comprehend scientifically whatever is\n[[818.21]] made capable of knowing. To compleat which the united Labours of many will be necessary\n[[818.22]] and of such as are fitly qualifyed and those often Meeting and Debating together, and exerting\n[[818.23]] their utmost abilitys in A right way. But where are these to be found. Either will or ability or\n[[818.24]] opportunity or some other necessary concomitant is found wanting. Soe that I fear this may be\n[[818.25]] seen in Speculation but twill be very difficult to bring it into act, and Every one must be content\n[[818.26]] to improve himself soe far as he can in the Disquisition on this or that subject he has most\n[[818.27]] present need of knowing. I question not but M^#'r Leibnitz may have many of these specimina by\n[[818.28]] him and therefore I doe heartily wish you could prevaile w^#'t^#'h him to Communicate some of these\n[[818.29]] which would be a means to persuade severall yet incredulous of the possibility of such a\n[[818.30]] Science: for my own part I Should very gladly contribute my Indeavours towards this end but\n[[818.31]] the Scarcity of Persons to converse w^#'t^#'h concerning it does almost Discourage me. But the\n[[819.1]] concurrence and confirmation of soe excellent a Person as Mon^#'r Leibnitz would be very\n[[819.2]] prevalent for making Proselyts. <Fn><i>Darunter von Hookes Hand</i>: concerning M^#'r Leibnitz his Dessigne for Universall Language or Characters sent by M^#'r Haak to M^#'r Leibnitz May 15, 1681.</Fn> </p>\n",
  "number": "231a.",
  "title": "ROBERT HOOKE AN THEODOR HAAK FÜR LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "[London, 13. April 1681.] [228a.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:231a. ROBERT HOOKE AN THEODOR HAAK FÜR LEIBNIZ [London, 13. April 1681.] [228a.] S^#'r I am extreamly pleasd to find soe excellent a Person as the Learned world must Acknowledg M^#'r Leibnitz to concur in the same opinion w^#'t^#'h me that A language somew^#'t Like that of y^#'e Bishop of Chester wo...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>